[{:db/id 17592186129176 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43229055-b652-5005-bf91-54dcfc3e2941"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128995 :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](images/85/8579b0afd584298a247c38af153d4e69945e73923e9605a168734c9250f3d18a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](images/11/11af9a5354d23586af399f9bfade0641e9bb10898068ea825755de5c645e3d9c.svg)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128926 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n![](images/56/564d16a59313514424d24b8c247d8a3516bfa32188292d2cbc7fee7faf2f5744.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n![](images/53/53977f4d27cf659f7d595afc4422b0c3009218fe836615eba5faf8a854124c6b.svg)\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/40/40fea7849f3603441671253bb7bc96e56be9bab6a8ddcbc94320238a0e3f529a.svg)\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/08/08ed315816def9b28fb3918a2dd103a5008815fc6a07507b64c5c20572b1c88f.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128925 :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n![](images/27/2701e789f5d3f6fc48fda87706add41ccb59c92d5bae4a76e84ac1abfdce6f07.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/d8/d8725937a4f5f1cfcd36cbe4871a872187df071b54c15d2e29d9b1e3c5f9b731.svg)\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/5e/5e3142b1ad4bb219db5d5b144e47fe8d1fa8d1f92c300c6f60fc145cf9424900.svg)\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/93/9331fdbede7da49e2dbbc66aac0b3084b1c7acca1ac7e789eded304956a18500.svg)\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/76/76e7add6349e0b2fceddf094ac6e3e8cfd0bf1bb43a3fbee0c143b256b81f1c5.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-17d0a606-b191-57ce-bda5-cb6bdd31b9a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128927 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n![](images/aa/aad9e35c3e07e67260a7f3ce96da685be97fab68fe542d262be0ed4f0941f909.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n![](images/f8/f89c32a7464b2eeb0f6db6a2c80feef98e8aa24d012b44695e7c7d24b91829ec.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-43229055-b652-5005-bf91-54dcfc3e2941" :question/id #uuid "43229055-b652-5005-bf91-54dcfc3e2941" :question/math-academy-id "q-129206" :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-6$, $4$, and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-6+4+1=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9abb4bdb-6a2c-505b-9dc2-250a89af5226"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9abb4bdb-6a2c-505b-9dc2-250a89af5226" :answer-field/id #uuid "9abb4bdb-6a2c-505b-9dc2-250a89af5226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-da23471b-f798-5486-86af-971ad557716d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da23471b-f798-5486-86af-971ad557716d" "answer-af01445c-3d84-5d24-87a3-64223a7372ab" "answer-de9eacf8-6e58-5082-9700-9ef1eaea5160" "answer-ba88dc80-baa7-5c24-9c66-3bc2e7c87798" "answer-d4778d8a-14c7-5354-8674-e0b3a10d2f71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da23471b-f798-5486-86af-971ad557716d" :answer/id #uuid "da23471b-f798-5486-86af-971ad557716d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af01445c-3d84-5d24-87a3-64223a7372ab" :answer/id #uuid "af01445c-3d84-5d24-87a3-64223a7372ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de9eacf8-6e58-5082-9700-9ef1eaea5160" :answer/id #uuid "de9eacf8-6e58-5082-9700-9ef1eaea5160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba88dc80-baa7-5c24-9c66-3bc2e7c87798" :answer/id #uuid "ba88dc80-baa7-5c24-9c66-3bc2e7c87798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4778d8a-14c7-5354-8674-e0b3a10d2f71" :answer/id #uuid "d4778d8a-14c7-5354-8674-e0b3a10d2f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0" :question/id #uuid "72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42005" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f91971d-c20c-5a76-a12b-2827ef0652b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f91971d-c20c-5a76-a12b-2827ef0652b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f91971d-c20c-5a76-a12b-2827ef0652b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-521a920f-2f8c-531a-965b-1cdb14e91dd0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf0253c3-f269-5021-82aa-caf40ced2760" "answer-1dc8f4a4-b6d6-5c99-bf78-b1f7a4d93a23" "answer-1d8d25d8-fe04-53ff-b342-7ebac143d4d5" "answer-18db0a49-6e70-5b48-904f-fb9b5f8f1167" "answer-521a920f-2f8c-531a-965b-1cdb14e91dd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf0253c3-f269-5021-82aa-caf40ced2760" :answer/id #uuid "bf0253c3-f269-5021-82aa-caf40ced2760" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dc8f4a4-b6d6-5c99-bf78-b1f7a4d93a23" :answer/id #uuid "1dc8f4a4-b6d6-5c99-bf78-b1f7a4d93a23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d8d25d8-fe04-53ff-b342-7ebac143d4d5" :answer/id #uuid "1d8d25d8-fe04-53ff-b342-7ebac143d4d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18db0a49-6e70-5b48-904f-fb9b5f8f1167" :answer/id #uuid "18db0a49-6e70-5b48-904f-fb9b5f8f1167" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-521a920f-2f8c-531a-965b-1cdb14e91dd0" :answer/id #uuid "521a920f-2f8c-531a-965b-1cdb14e91dd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38" :question/id #uuid "a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38" :question/math-academy-id "q-129230" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-848d2bf5-7181-5403-afac-d10425ef5d8c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-848d2bf5-7181-5403-afac-d10425ef5d8c" :answer-field/id #uuid "848d2bf5-7181-5403-afac-d10425ef5d8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3fd4fdcb-52a1-577b-9cee-a9fa9d18334b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9c227b1-80fa-5ed1-8fcb-7bbadbc92d9f" "answer-12f4ffe3-c54b-5dec-af7e-f3eb29c5efac" "answer-0bcbaf3a-7d79-5c34-9970-8e30a0164f3d" "answer-3fd4fdcb-52a1-577b-9cee-a9fa9d18334b" "answer-42122353-59f4-5dee-9867-47f69bf794e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9c227b1-80fa-5ed1-8fcb-7bbadbc92d9f" :answer/id #uuid "e9c227b1-80fa-5ed1-8fcb-7bbadbc92d9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12f4ffe3-c54b-5dec-af7e-f3eb29c5efac" :answer/id #uuid "12f4ffe3-c54b-5dec-af7e-f3eb29c5efac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bcbaf3a-7d79-5c34-9970-8e30a0164f3d" :answer/id #uuid "0bcbaf3a-7d79-5c34-9970-8e30a0164f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fd4fdcb-52a1-577b-9cee-a9fa9d18334b" :answer/id #uuid "3fd4fdcb-52a1-577b-9cee-a9fa9d18334b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42122353-59f4-5dee-9867-47f69bf794e2" :answer/id #uuid "42122353-59f4-5dee-9867-47f69bf794e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-17d0a606-b191-57ce-bda5-cb6bdd31b9a8" :question/id #uuid "17d0a606-b191-57ce-bda5-cb6bdd31b9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42373" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{32}$, ${a}_{43}$ and ${a}_{44}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c9772538-fd34-5f2a-b5f8-a7d295110074"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9772538-fd34-5f2a-b5f8-a7d295110074" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9772538-fd34-5f2a-b5f8-a7d295110074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2231485a-d292-515f-b51b-91f31ecd0efe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5bcd7de-6ec8-511e-9e85-d25e1afb7c50" "answer-dbd6ae2c-f7e4-5a2b-9120-ea5f2f442053" "answer-82eb2341-c973-51c4-a691-9aab4038100d" "answer-2231485a-d292-515f-b51b-91f31ecd0efe" "answer-0e03e0f4-f6d8-5e5e-be1b-2065040084b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5bcd7de-6ec8-511e-9e85-d25e1afb7c50" :answer/id #uuid "a5bcd7de-6ec8-511e-9e85-d25e1afb7c50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{22}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbd6ae2c-f7e4-5a2b-9120-ea5f2f442053" :answer/id #uuid "dbd6ae2c-f7e4-5a2b-9120-ea5f2f442053" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{43}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82eb2341-c973-51c4-a691-9aab4038100d" :answer/id #uuid "82eb2341-c973-51c4-a691-9aab4038100d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{32}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2231485a-d292-515f-b51b-91f31ecd0efe" :answer/id #uuid "2231485a-d292-515f-b51b-91f31ecd0efe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{32}$, ${a}_{43}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e03e0f4-f6d8-5e5e-be1b-2065040084b9" :answer/id #uuid "0e03e0f4-f6d8-5e5e-be1b-2065040084b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{43}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130339 :tutorial/content "Consider the following matrices:\n![](images/10/1074870d255109821b5f36eb517f22531efbd8f5069f05c3de3f111b38befd02.svg)\n\nThe first non-zero entry on each row (from left to right) is called the **leading entry** of that row.\n\n- In the matrix $A,$ the leading entries are $a_{11}=2,$ $a_{22}=3,$ $a_{32}=1,$ and $a_{43}=5.$\n\n- In the matrix $B,$ the leading entries are $b_{11}=1,$ $b_{22}=3,$ $b_{33}=-2,$ and $b_{44}=2.$ The $5$th row has no leading entry.\n\nThe leading entries are highlighted below.\n\n![](images/6b/6b1d99269c847f7c6bc0558da347fb300dba5fa6caf373cd1ed5cc5ebacb1649.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130380 :tutorial/content "Let's consider our matrices $A$ and $B$ once more, with the leading entries highlighted.\n\n![](images/af/af61f32297e248ab9989ba59ea6c9bda2f99efe19d25df525fef916617843a32.svg)\n\nWe say that a matrix is in **row echelon form** if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nHere, $B$ is in row echelon form since both conditions are satisfied. However, $A$ is not in row echelon form since condition II is violated: the leading entry of the third row $(a_{32}={\\color{red}1})$ is placed just below the leading entry of the second row $(a_{22}=3).$\n\nGenerally speaking, row echelon form means that we have *stairs* where each step (represented by a leading entry $\\bbox[lightgray, 3pt]{\\large\\ast}$) has a height of $1.$\n\n![](images/67/67f83c454e59d16ae80cf67a19b19f968182251a2e5d1b405e2c422e0313d5b7.png)\n\nFinally, an *augmented* matrix is in row echelon form if the coefficient matrix (i.e., the part that is to the left of the vertical bar) is in row echelon form." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129395 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
